Of course. I will add a complete purchase order management system to your application. This will allow you to create, track, and receive purchase orders directly within the app, which will automatically update your stock levels.

This is a significant feature, so I've been careful to integrate it seamlessly without disrupting any of your existing functionality. The new "Purchasing" section will only be visible to users with the 'Admin' role.

Here are the changes I'm making:

1.  **New "Purchasing" Hub:** I've added a new "Purchasing" section to both the desktop sidebar and the mobile navigation bar for admin users. This is the central place for all purchase order activities.
2.  **Purchase Order Management:**
    *   **List View:** The main screen of the new section shows a list of all your purchase orders, with at-a-glance details like status, supplier, and total value.
    *   **Creation Form:** You can create new purchase orders by selecting a supplier and adding items from your existing `Item Types`. The form is intuitive and calculates costs automatically.
    *   **Detailed View:** Clicking on any purchase order takes you to a detailed view where you can see all the information and items for that order.
3.  **Integrated "Goods In" Process:**
    *   From the detailed view of an "Ordered" PO, you can initiate the "Receive Stock" process.
    *   For standard items, you simply enter the quantity you've received.
    *   For unique, serialized items (like meters), the system will prompt you to use the barcode scanner to scan each individual item as you receive it, ensuring perfect tracking.
    *   Once you confirm the receipt, your main stock inventory is **automatically updated**, and the purchase order status changes to "Partially Received" or "Completed".

I have defined the necessary database structure in the code. Before you run the app with these changes, you will need to execute the following SQL in your Supabase SQL Editor to create the required tables for the purchasing system to function correctly.

```sql
-- Create the purchase_orders table
CREATE TABLE public.purchase_orders (
    id bigint NOT NULL,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    user_id uuid NOT NULL,
    supplier_id bigint NOT NULL,
    status text DEFAULT 'Draft'::text NOT NULL,
    order_date timestamp with time zone,
    notes text,
    po_number text
);

ALTER TABLE public.purchase_orders ALTER COLUMN id ADD GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY (
    SEQUENCE NAME public.purchase_orders_id_seq
    START WITH 1
    INCREMENT BY 1
    NO MINVALUE
    NO MAXVALUE
    CACHE 1
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX purchase_orders_pkey ON public.purchase_orders USING btree (id);
ALTER TABLE public.purchase_orders ADD CONSTRAINT purchase_orders_pkey PRIMARY KEY USING INDEX purchase_orders_pkey;
ALTER TABLE public.purchase_orders ADD CONSTRAINT purchase_orders_supplier_id_fkey FOREIGN KEY (supplier_id) REFERENCES public.suppliers(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT;
ALTER TABLE public.purchase_orders ADD CONSTRAINT purchase_orders_user_id_fkey FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE;

-- Create the purchase_order_items table
CREATE TABLE public.purchase_order_items (
    id bigint NOT NULL,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    user_id uuid NOT NULL,
    po_id bigint NOT NULL,
    item_type_id bigint NOT NULL,
    quantity_ordered integer DEFAULT 0 NOT NULL,
    quantity_received integer DEFAULT 0 NOT NULL,
    cost_per_item numeric DEFAULT 0 NOT NULL
);

ALTER TABLE public.purchase_order_items ALTER COLUMN id ADD GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY (
    SEQUENCE NAME public.purchase_order_items_id_seq
    START WITH 1
    INCREMENT BY 1
    NO MINVALUE
    NO MAXVALUE
    CACHE 1
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX purchase_order_items_pkey ON public.purchase_order_items USING btree (id);
ALTER TABLE public.purchase_order_items ADD CONSTRAINT purchase_order_items_pkey PRIMARY KEY USING INDEX purchase_order_items_pkey;
ALTER TABLE public.purchase_order_items ADD CONSTRAINT purchase_order_items_item_type_id_fkey FOREIGN KEY (item_type_id) REFERENCES public.item_types(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT;
ALTER TABLE public.purchase_order_items ADD CONSTRAINT purchase_order_items_po_id_fkey FOREIGN KEY (po_id) REFERENCES public.purchase_orders(id) ON DELETE CASCADE;
ALTER TABLE public.purchase_order_items ADD CONSTRAINT purchase_order_items_user_id_fkey FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE;

-- Enable Row Level Security (RLS)
ALTER TABLE public.purchase_orders ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.purchase_order_items ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Create RLS policies
CREATE POLICY "Enable all access for authenticated users" ON public.purchase_orders FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = user_id) WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);
CREATE POLICY "Enable all access for authenticated users" ON public.purchase_order_items FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = user_id) WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);
```

Here are the code updates for the application itself.

